        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How and when are action-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You may score several in a turn but only one per combat or step: one in a space combat and another in the ground combat that follows is fine, two from the same combat is not.&rdquo; only one secret objective per combat, so Fight with Precision uses up that combat&rsquo;s scoring.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Scoring <i>Fight with Precision &Omega;</i> will count as that player&rsquo;s single secret objective scoring for that combat.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How and when are action-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You may score several in a turn but only one per combat or step: one in a space combat and another in the ground combat that follows is fine, two from the same combat is not.&rdquo; only one secret objective per combat, so Fight with Precision uses up that combat&rsquo;s scoring.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The action cards must be discarded during the status phase. Any action cards that were discarded during the action phase will have no effect.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When do I discard the 5 action cards for Form a Spy Network?&rdquo;: &ldquo;When you score it in the status phase, as its cost, without resolving the cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_hacan">Hacan</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Emirates_of_Hacan#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Guild%20Ships"><sc>Guild Ships</sc></a> faction ability does not make a player neighbors with all other players.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who counts as my neighbor?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Hacan can transact with non-neighbors, and anyone can with them, but that doesn&rsquo;t make them neighbors for Pillage.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has units or controls a planet in a system containing an alpha wormhole, and the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player has units or controls a planet in a system containing a beta wormhole, or vice versa, those two players are neighbors.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who counts as my neighbor?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Players with a unit or controlled planet in the same system or adjacent systems, wormholes included.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The resources must be spent during the status phase. Any resources that were spent during the action phase will have no effect.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;For objectives that require spending resources, influence, tokens or trade goods, does earlier spending count?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; you pay the full amount in one go when you score the objective, as its cost; nothing spent earlier in the round counts.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Trade goods may be spent as resources when scoring <i>Found a Golden Age</i>.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Trade goods can stand in for resources or influence there, though a &lsquo;spend trade goods&rsquo; objective needs actual trade goods.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The command tokens must be spent during the status phase. Any command tokens that were spent during the action phase will have no effect.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;For objectives that require spending resources, influence, tokens or trade goods, does earlier spending count?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; you pay the full amount in one go when you score the objective, as its cost; nothing spent earlier in the round counts.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The influence, resources and trade goods must be spent during the status phase. Any that were spent during the action phase will have no effect.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;For objectives that require spending resources, influence, tokens or trade goods, does earlier spending count?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; you pay the full amount in one go when you score the objective, as its cost; nothing spent earlier in the round counts.&rdquo;</li>
